# Cursor rules for Stickman-Videos

Read AGENT_INSTRUCTIONS.md at the repository root before writing or changing any
code that touches a frame.

- The repo is Python (PIL, numpy). TypeScript/JS animation code pasted from a
  ticket describes an *effect*; translate the constraint, never the file.
- No faces on stickman heads, no drawn close-up faces, no comic stars, no
  sine-wave limbs, no stacked idle enemies, no attacks while down.
- Always commit and tag a restore point (`restore/<name>`) before a batch of
  risky changes.
- Verify with pixels and numbers before claiming a fix.
